##### DIAGNOSE (before fix)
$ node lab/02-blocked-reply/diagnose.mjs
customer dana@example.com (eafa9170-84d8-4635-956b-93dbc8d994c2) replies on her own ticket #9 "Upgrade did not unlock recurring invoices" (assignee_id: 5f029bd9-0180-405a-8984-da898694675e)

=== 1. What the client receives ===
HTTP 403 Forbidden
{
  "code": "42501",
  "details": null,
  "hint": null,
  "message": "new row violates row-level security policy for table \"messages\""
}

=== 2. Is it a missing table privilege? (that would say "permission denied for table") ===
{ authenticated_can_insert: true }

=== 3. INSERT policies on public.messages (pg_policies) ===
messages: reply on tickets you work on  PERMISSIVE roles={authenticated}
  WITH CHECK ((author_id = ( SELECT auth.uid() AS uid)) AND (( SELECT private.is_agent() AS is_agent) OR ((is_internal = false) AND (ticket_id IN ( SELECT tickets.id
   FROM tickets
  WHERE (tickets.assignee_id = ( SELECT auth.uid() AS uid)))))))

=== 4. Each condition of the WITH CHECK, evaluated as the customer for the row she sent ===
{
  author_is_caller: true,
  not_internal: true,
  caller_is_agent: false,
  ticket_assigned_to_caller: false,
  ticket_owned_by_caller: true
}
(exit 0)

